# Metrics declared in construct-metrics that nothing in the workspace writes.
#
# Checked by scripts/check-observability.py. A RATCHET, not a budget: a new
# unwritten metric fails the check, a line left here after the metric gains a
# producer fails, and a line naming a metric that no longer exists fails. The
# list may only shrink.
#
# ── EMPTY, and that is the point ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# It held sixteen entries when it was created on 2026-08-13, because nineteen of
# the Grafana overview's 27 panels read metrics that no code path could fill.
# Emptied the same day:
#
#   instrumented — construct_otpk_{uploaded,consumed}_total in key-service, plus
#     construct_otpk_devices_{total,low,exhausted} from a 60s inventory poll;
#     construct_grpc_streams_active and the opened/closed counters in
#     messaging-service.
#
#   deleted — the five session-lifecycle metrics and KT proof failures, because
#     those events happen inside the E2EE envelope and only a client could
#     report them, which is telemetry we do not collect; the two TURN
#     placeholders, because coturn holds those numbers and the answer is an
#     exporter; the three gateway request metrics, because the gateway stopped
#     proxying the API and Caddy now reports per-request latency and status.
#
# Keep it empty. If a metric belongs here, it needs a reason written next to it,
# and the reason has to survive being read aloud.
